Z||000039||Formula88||11-14-2001||04:59 PM||||Well, it's hard to say.  If you wing it, I like the black wing.  The raised wing is better than a stock height, because the stock height wing blocks the lines of the scoop.  I'm leaning towards the wing - possibly even raised just a tad more - to make sure you can see the scoop from underneath the wing.<P>You've definately got one of the most original Fiero's around, girl.  No one's gonna mistake yours for someone elses.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And I love the double takes you get when you tell people it's an 87 while they're looking at the bumper pad front and rear fascias.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000040||Tina||11-14-2001||05:19 PM||||Great Guys,we are evenly split here.<BR>14 yes <BR>14 no<BR>5  assorted<P>But changing scoop is not an option,<BR>(need the room)<BR>as to changing the looks to a later coupe with different nose, round moldings e.t.c.<P>(Hold on here, zipping up the flamesuit)<P>It is actually an 87, but I swapped the panels,(prefer the 84 look).<BR>Forget now who said it,but yes, those stantions are too close to the scoop.<BR>That's one thing that bugs me, the other how it looks from the side.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>BTW While on the subject,what do you tall Fiero wing Owners use for the gasket (between  stantions and decklid)?<BR>||||reg||1
