Z||000042||SLAMMED87GT||11-14-2001||07:26 PM||||Hi Tina, How's it going?? I of course have the 7" stands and stock wing, and I like the taller ones. I say get 7" stands and paint the wing to match. <P>And then buckle up becasue you might take off with the V8!!!!<P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||10
Z||000043||kevin||11-14-2001||07:38 PM||||NO wing! There I think I broke the tie. The combination of the scoop(BIG) and the wing (LARGE)over exaggerates the beauty of the stock lines. Leave the scoop, cuz you got a V-8 under there and surprise them when you hit 130 mph with a smile on your face. THe aerodynamics of the Fiero is safe at that velocity. Your best attribute is the cool side scoops. Where did you get those? How much? E-mail me PVmeans@CS.com||||reg||1
Z||000044||4BanGinFun||11-14-2001||08:03 PM||||i think the wing looks cool i have an 85 se with the rack right now but i am looking for a nice spoiler for it i think the spoiler is nice on that car black but maybe move it back a bit so the trailing edge of the wing is a bit farther back the the tail lights prolly even with the bumper or less||||reg||1
Z||000045||Bazooka||11-14-2001||08:08 PM||||Tina,    I used a 3/16" thick Rubber Sheet that was provided by the Maker of the Raised Wing Stanchions (Fiero Conversions, Inc.). The material can be found at Plumbers and HVAC supply stores since it is used as a vibration and sound deterant. <BR>   The best way to determine whether to use the wing or not, is to actually set one up on your decklid if you can borrow it. I was doubtful of the spatial relationship too until I set up the prop. It makes good use of the whole decklid to have the scoop vents and the wing back there. The only question that I have is "Would the setup look better if the scoop openings could be extended more to the rear so that they terminate under the wing somewhere? Just my thoughts. My twin snorkels do that and I'm pleased with the way they look. Go girl!<BR>**********************************<BR>BTW While on the subject,what do you tall Fiero wing Owners use for the gasket (between stantions and decklid)?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000046||86seyellow||11-14-2001||08:45 PM||||Tina, <P>Well I think you hsould do what you like. I personally like yoru wing way to much. I can imagine your wing on my car. The wing is the height I need , the color and everythign. The minute I saw it saturday night I wanted it. So , if you decide to nix the wing, I will no doubt want it from you. I wont even have to repaint it.. &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;<P>SO , you decide and if you need to let it go . Let me have the option of being the person to take it. Thank you<P>ROn -86seyellow.<P>If you giv eme the wing I will work on the talking BArry White for your car!!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86seyellow_new1.JPG"> <BR>All Stock plus goodies||||reg||1
Z||000047||Tina||11-14-2001||09:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 86seyellow:<BR><B>If you give me the wing I will work on the talking Barry White for your car!!!!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Oh..., great man,now you have done it.<BR>I won't be able to get rid of <B>that voice</B> for a while again.<P>Tina (still undecided)<BR>BTW ...but if I decide to nix it, I give you a call  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000048||86seyellow||11-14-2001||10:14 PM||||"HEY BAbY....... YOU NEED TO NITROUS ME!!<P>"MOVE OVER AND LET ME HELP YOU OUT WITH ALL THIS PERFORANCE" <P>HEY BABY, U NEED TO ROCK MY WORLD.<P>How is that Tina. No I realy will help with the Barry white thing. I can rig soemthign up like the 80s chryselrs that talked. Somethng like, HEY BABY&lt; SHUT THE DOOR&lt; I DONt NEEDYOU GETTING TO COLD, or BABY MY BATTERY IS GETTTING LOW&lt; WOULD YOU JUMP ME!!<P>What think TIna<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86seyellow_new1.JPG"> <BR>All Stock plus goodies||||reg||1
Z||000049||Philphine||11-14-2001||10:18 PM||||compleatly wierd idea, but i see it in my head and i like it. the scoop is so big it's like there isn't enought room aestheticly (rasslin' with the big words) for a wing. so make the scoop even bigger and make the wing part of it.<P>say you have and extra trunk lid. maybe graft on a big cowl induction type scoop like an old chevelle would have. maybe about 3" high. going from the front to back of the lid (with just a hole in the front part where you need it). i think there's one in the photo gallery like that. then you don't need stanteons. you could put the wing right on the scoop, which would look kind of tacky. or you could mold the wing into the end of the scoop so it looks kind of like fins. sorta.<P>like i said, i like it better in my head than trying to describe it, but if you've got the parts around (seems like you run in some circles were someone you know might have the cowl induction scoop) to just set  on the back of a wingless/scoopless fiero and eyeball it, maybe it will look better than the description.the one bad thing i can think of is if the scoop is much higher than a few inches, you'd have a big blind spot if you couldn't see over it. give it some thought. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000050||RossT||11-15-2001||05:02 AM||||Normally I like the wing, but I don't think it looks good with the scoop!!||||reg||1
Z||000051||87GTZ34||11-15-2001||10:19 AM||||Unwing it!  Your car looks more unique and kick-a$$ without the wing.||||reg||1
